.Sh DESCRIPTION
SHA-3 (Secure Hash Algorithm 3) is a family of cryptographic hash
functions standardized in NIST FIPS 202, first published in 2015. It is
based on the Keccak algorithm.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_sha3_224(), EVP_sha3_256(), EVP_sha3_384(), EVP_sha3_512()
The SHA-3 SHA-3-224, SHA-3-256, SHA-3-384, and SHA-3-512 algorithms
respectively.
They produce 224, 256, 384 and 512 bits of output from a given input.
.It EVP_shake128(), EVP_shake256()
The SHAKE-128 and SHAKE-256 Extendable Output Functions (XOF) that can
generate a variable hash length.
.Pp
Specifically,
.Sy EVP_shake128
provides an overall security of 128 bits, while
.Sy EVP_shake256
provides that of 256 bits.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Developers should be aware of the negative performance implications of
calling these functions multiple times and should consider using
.Xr EVP_MD_fetch 3
with
.Xr EVP_MD-SHA3 7
or
.Xr EVP_MD-SHAKE 7
instead.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return a
.Sy EVP_MD
structure that contains the implementation of the message digest.
See
.Xr EVP_MD_meth_new 3
for details of the
.Sy EVP_MD
structure.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
NIST FIPS 202.
